$native_attribution## Product context

Merman targets compatibility with a pinned Mermaid.js release. Pele supplies its own layout and visual style. Mermaid v13 discovers diagram plugins in the Node consumer. The Mermaid CLI uses a browser to write files. [Merman compatibility](https://github.com/Latias94/merman#rendering-quality-and-performance) · [Pele design](https://github.com/obsidianmd/pele/tree/1.13.0#compatibility) · [Mermaid v13](https://github.com/mermaid-js/mermaid-v13) · [Mermaid CLI](https://github.com/mermaid-js/mermaid-cli)

Separate measurements compare native renderers and changes between Merman releases. [Native Merman and mmdr comparison](https://github.com/Latias94/merman/blob/main/docs/performance/renderer_comparison_2026-07-28_75c9fd156_vs_mmdr.md) · [Same-implementation release evidence](https://github.com/Latias94/merman/blob/main/docs/release/RELEASE_REPORTS.md)

## Reproduce this report

The portable receipt records the measured builds, workload fingerprints and observations. For each eligible Node timing pair it includes both workers' batch medians and their within-round ratio. [Portable measurement receipt]($receipt). $raw_bundle

To regenerate the Markdown beside the receipt, run this command from the repository root with the downloaded JSON path. For the original wording of an archived report, use the generator and template from its publication revision.

```console
python tools/bench/bench.py report --from path/to/measurements.json
```

Add `--check` to verify an existing Markdown file. To collect a new run, match the product versions, inputs, settings and sample counts for the operation you want to compare. [Measurement contract](https://github.com/Latias94/merman/blob/main/docs/performance/BENCHMARKING.md) · [Collection and publication procedure](https://github.com/Latias94/merman/blob/main/docs/performance/RUNBOOK.md#publish-a-reader-report)
